/**
 * Linux/systemd server install.
 *
 * Side effects go through InstallHost. TLS and the 0.x store are generated by
 * loadOrCreateTls, NmzpStore.load, and bootstrapAdmin inside a root-owned seed
 * directory, then copied. Existing tls material and admin.token are never
 * overwritten. Trust for "this install created the tree" lives in root-owned
 * /etc/nmzp/install-state.json, not in the nmzp-writable data directory.
 *
 * Residual risk: Node has no openat2. After this process closes a directory fd,
 * nmzp (who owns the data directory) can still replace a child such as tls/
 * before the next open. Ancestors of --data are rejected unless they are
 * root-owned and not group/world writable, which closes that swap above the
 * data directory.
 */
